entries.purpose:
Frozen tectonic conditioning for the physical TD checkpoint.

All queries use absolute coordinates. The product's finite rectangle is enforced;
its bilinear interpolation still wraps across the last half-cell at the edge.

Quasi-steady rectangular-channel stages on a shared distributary DAG.

Manning friction and critical-depth controls are engineering approximations;
no floodplain storage, momentum balance or calibrated cross sections are solved.

Statistical tidal windows for finite-source distributary formation.

Each equal-weight phase represents a fraction of equivalent geological time;
physical event time is unchanged. This is not a tidal hydrodynamic model.
